refused: d273_size_says_bytes.cy:7:67, line 7 column 67
 7 |     let mut $out: os::stdout.buffered = os::stdout.buffered(size: 1024);
   |                                                                   ^^^^
 fix:  `1024 bytes`
 why:  `os::stdout` and `os::stderr` say which kind they are: `.buffered(size: 1024 bytes)` writes in chunks and is finished with `os::done`, and `.unbuffered()` writes each print straight away (D273)

refused: d273_size_says_bytes.cy:8:5, line 8 column 5
 8 |     os::done(Give $out);
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 what: `$out` never got a value
 why:  a variable is read only after it has one (D203)
 because: d273_size_says_bytes.cy:7:67, line 7 column 67
 7 |     let mut $out: os::stdout.buffered = os::stdout.buffered(size: 1024);
   |                                                                   ^^^^
     with `1024 bytes` here, this error goes away
